menu "e32p: obd2"

    config E32P_OBD2_ENABLE
        bool "Enable e32p_obd2 (SAE J1979 / ISO 15765-4 OBD-II services)"
        depends on SOC_TWAI_SUPPORTED
        select E32P_ISOTP_ENABLE
        default n
        help
            OBD-II services over ISO-TP: current data (0x01), freeze frame
            (0x02), stored and pending trouble codes (0x03 / 0x07), clear
            (0x04), and vehicle information (0x09).

            The service layer is pure - one request in, one response out, with
            no clock and no bus - so every service is testable headless. Only
            the thin transport glue touches ISO-TP.

    config E32P_OBD2_MAX_DTC
        int "Diagnostic trouble codes the store holds"
        depends on E32P_OBD2_ENABLE
        range 1 32
        default 10
        help
            Each code costs 3 bytes of RAM and 5 characters in the NVS string
            that survives a reset. A real ECU holds far more; 10 is enough for
            a demo and keeps the store one short write.

endmenu
